WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.920
Nintendo World Cup.

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:03.420
Pass. Shoot.

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:06.420
Score! It's world class fun!

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:13.060
Nintendo World Cup.

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:30.500
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:31.660
I'm Mike.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:45.020
And I'm Sean. And this is our first time we're recording in 2026, which is kind of timely because, Sean, there is a World Cup happening this year and in America, no less.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:49.620
I guess it was like a 25% chance that that was going to happen.

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:51.240
Well, I guess not the American one.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:53.840
Yeah. Yeah, that's like the crazy one.

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:55.980
Yeah. But it's also like messy.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:58.740
It's not really just the United States.

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:04.620
It's technically America because it's all North America, but there's some games in Canada, some games in Mexico.

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:09.020
Shouldn't all the games just be at MetLife Stadium and just call it a day?

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:12.060
Oh, I was.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.760
Actually, that's what I thought it was going to be.

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:19.680
So you actually made me feel better in terms of traffic and amount of people.

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:21.040
So. Yeah. No.

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:27.640
Well, don't worry. You can still consider Airbnb-ing your apartment for this summer.

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:29.040
For $4,000 a night?

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:31.380
Yeah. $4,000 a night sounds about right.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:38.380
Okay. Now, in 1990, when this game came out, there was also a World Cup.

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:42.520
And the real World Cup in 1990 was held in Italy.

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:55.240
West Germany defeated the defending champions Argentina, won nothing in a final that ended on a late penalty in West Germany's favor.

00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:02.180
And that's kind of like the story of the whole World Cup is that it was a defensive, low-scoring World Cup.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:06.560
There were only an average of 2.2 goals per game.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:09.180
And I'm like, well, 2.2 actually sounds pretty high.

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:11.520
A lot of these games end in 1-0, right?

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:15.620
It kind of reminds me of like the dead puck era.

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:21.740
Yes. In hockey where, you know, everything was just 1-0, 1-1, you know.

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:23.100
So there's the dead puck.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:25.220
There was also dead ball in baseball.

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:26.820
So this was its own dead ball. Right, right.

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:29.560
What is football's deflate gate?

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:37.480
There is a word that's used for like the low-scoring era.

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:40.840
I forgot what it's called though, but it has one.

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:43.520
I think it was in the 50s or 60s.

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:53.560
Maybe more importantly for the 1990 World Cup though is that the United States is back in the 1990 World Cup for the first time since 1950.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:03:02.980
So that's probably why this game is also like being licensed for the NES as like a Nintendo World Cup.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:06.800
Get this to North America because it's not this game on the Famicom.

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:15.680
No. And so there's like a push there probably to be like, well, we got to capitalize on this moment because soccer is kind of back in.

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:19.780
And people always say that by the way, soccer is on the rise and everything.

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:25.140
Is it really? No, I don't think it's ever truly going to be on the rise here.

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:26.340
It's fine. Here, right.

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:27.660
Here specifically. Yes.

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:36.160
I mean, I think more people care about like Premier League and that stuff than they ever are going to care about like MLS.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:40.180
And I do think that like, you know, there is more interest in MLS these days.

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:51.280
But if you look at the like if we're looking at as a horse race between MLS and even not even just not even NFL because that's not even a fair comparison.

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:55.820
But but even baseball, then I think that it's losing.

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:57.220
It's losing track there, too.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:58.400
You know? Yeah.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:07.960
Funny you mentioned that, too, because baseball was just soccer beat out baseball in a recent poll of my favorite sports.

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:11.180
And it was 10 percent of people's favorite sport.

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:14.180
So it's it's ahead of baseball now.

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:16.460
Well, you just countered my claim.

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:18.360
No, no. But think about this for a second.

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:21.240
OK, so the question is, what's your favorite sport?

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.320
Right. So obviously, a lot of people are saying football.

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:24.760
Some people are saying basketball.

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:26.980
And then it kind of gets divvied out between the rest.

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:33.320
But I would argue that a lot of people who say football or basketball would probably say baseball is like their number two.

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:38.220
Right. So it's like no one's saying the people who are saying soccer is their favorite are insane.

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:44.440
And then and then like they wouldn't those same people like nobody who watches the NFL is putting soccer as their number two.

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:47.080
They're putting it at like I forgot that this sport existed.

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:55.660
You know, there's got to be some word for the statistical analysis of these kinds of preferential rankings.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:58.620
But I think you got a speed on that one.

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:03.060
Yeah. So let's see.

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:04.320
Where was I going with this, though?

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:22.560
Because oh, yeah. So the the low scoring defensive World Cup of 1990 is juxtaposed by this Nintendo World Cup video game where it is five on five arcade soccer where you're encouraged to absolutely destroy your opponents.

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:23.820
There are no fouls.

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:25.300
There are no offsides.

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:29.000
Players get knocked unconscious and they just lie dead on the field.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:35.700
Yeah. Yes. Every team has like super shots to do like really crazy trick shots.

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:38.980
And it's actually in Japan.

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:41.460
It's a Kunio Kun game.

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:45.720
One of those the same ones who did the dodgeball and River City Ransom.

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:48.600
This was a soccer game.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:54.680
I'm sorry if I say I have to say soccer going forward because if I say football, I think I'm going to confuse our primary audience.

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:59.060
Yeah. But yeah, I apologize to the two percent of you in Brazil.

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:01.060
You are appreciated.

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:14.600
So how funny is it that the real 1990 World Cup was ultra defensive and low scoring while Nintendo World Cup basically rewards you for transforming matches into, you know, demolition derbies?

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:16.680
It's it's it's it's fun.

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:31.280
I'm sort of sort of thinking like, oh, if there ever was an MLS hits or an MLS blitz, then this would be it.

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:34.720
It's just, you know, it's basically how I play FIFA.

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:43.620
I don't really know anything about formations or how to do or how to make an approach around a defense.

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:50.380
So I will just spam the slide tackle button and I end up getting yellow cards left and right.

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:55.000
This is me playing soccer with like freedom.

00:06:55.000 --> 00:07:08.540
And I think when you consider that this was part of the Cuneo series, I don't think that that's surprising to us anymore because of how we've covered it so frequently on this show with the ports and everything.

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:19.620
But also by now, I think in general, you know, people who bought a lot of NES games might catch on to this because the graphics are now a giveaway.

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:24.760
They continue to use the same sprite look across all of these games.

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:38.520
And so you do recognize that like, hey, like those are the same people from the dodgeball game or, you know, it's it's like the fact that they keep this consistent look and that they don't change even the look of the characters when they localize it.

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:49.120
I think helps make that connection even more obvious now than just some like, you know, chubby cherub situation where it was like it was based on a manga in Japan and they changed the whole thing to Cupid.

00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:50.580
Like that was a total redesign.

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:59.120
For me, the thing that actually threw me off wasn't so much the style, which I think is iconic.

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:04.340
It's just that the game itself is it's just Nintendo World Cup.

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:11.540
Like it's not it's not saying that it's of dodgeball fame or of River City Ransom fame.

00:08:11.540 --> 00:08:17.180
It's just this generic name for a game that otherwise is a very unique look.

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:18.380
It's very strange.

00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:31.600
Yeah, because the Famicom game had a whole like high school component to it where it was like Cuneo and his classmates are rivaling against like a bunch of other schools in a tournament.

00:08:31.720 --> 00:08:34.780
And there's like there's like a story there.

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:37.380
The story scenes are stripped out completely.

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:46.140
And instead that the high school teams are replaced with, you know, 13 national teams, Argentina, Brazil, Cameroon.

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:50.600
Yeah, I was going to ask, is Cameroon in the new World Cup?

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:52.680
Yeah, I don't know, actually.

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:55.840
And I did. I do have because I just wanted to see who the U.S.

00:08:55.860 --> 00:08:57.560
was playing first. And it's Paraguay.

00:08:57.700 --> 00:08:59.540
So we hate Paraguay right now.

00:08:59.820 --> 00:09:01.260
All my homies hate Paraguay.

00:09:01.420 --> 00:09:02.680
Yeah, they're next on the list.

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:06.620
Cameroon, though, I don't see on here.

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:07.860
So no, probably.

00:09:08.660 --> 00:09:10.520
Well, you know who else you don't see on this list?

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:12.160
West Germany.

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:15.620
I don't see West Germany competing in 2026 either.

00:09:16.060 --> 00:09:24.740
Damn. You know what's funny about that is West Germany, you know, the German reunification happened later in the same year.

00:09:24.740 --> 00:09:30.140
So it's like, I think even by the time we're in December now of 1990, it's probably already happened.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:33.940
So the game like releases and West Germany is not even really a country anymore.

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:47.100
It happens, you know, like I could see, like I think we've had some Soviet stuff in the last kind of months of the NES library.

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:48.880
So maybe, well, that's all right.

00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:51.140
It hasn't happened yet. So we'll get there.

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:52.700
Not the same thing.

00:09:52.860 --> 00:10:04.380
But I think about like the board game Risk 2 always had like a non-realistic map where like certain countries were just like entire regions instead.

00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:05.260
And it's like, well, hold on.

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:08.140
There's a couple of other countries, you know, like they simplify the game a little bit.

00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:13.300
But I remember like Ukraine just being a massive chunk of land going like all the way down to Greece.

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:15.980
And it's like, I didn't know it was that big.

00:10:15.980 --> 00:10:17.020
But I guess, yeah, right.

00:10:17.980 --> 00:10:20.540
Alt universe, Ukraine's taken over.

00:10:20.600 --> 00:10:22.460
I'm sure there's no New Zealand on the map either.

00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:24.880
Yeah, no New Zealand to even capture.

00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:30.440
That's true. I think now modern day Risk actually does do it with all the countries.

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:34.920
But who knows? Maybe it's like, I remember also that there was times where they just didn't even label countries.

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:38.020
It was like Northern Europe, Eastern Europe, Western Europe.

00:10:38.300 --> 00:10:40.260
That one is how I think I've played it.

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:44.140
Yeah. So there is no Western Europe team on here too.

00:10:44.140 --> 00:10:52.900
Anyway, the teams, it's the kind of thing where for me, when I see the team selection, I think it doesn't matter until I find out that it does.

00:10:52.900 --> 00:10:57.640
Because each of these teams has a different special shot.

00:10:57.640 --> 00:11:10.940
The one thing in this game to change the play style is that when you press the A and the B button together while taking a shot, you have the opportunity to do the super shot.

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:13.780
And that changes depending on what team you pick.

00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:16.020
So I guess there is some strategy there.

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:24.300
Yeah, and it also is another, like it looks exactly like the special shots in Dodgeball, like the way that they animate.

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:42.940
Whether it turns into like a hyper anime disc, like again, like as like a super shot in Dodgeball or as I think the United States has just like that kind of stylized spinning disc shot.

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:46.540
So it's another connection there.

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:51.320
Yeah, there are people doing like backflips and hitting the ball in the air.

00:11:51.660 --> 00:11:52.960
There's the headbutts.

00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:54.940
All great stuff.

00:11:54.940 --> 00:12:07.920
The story being removed from the Famicom version of the game and just now having it be like this loose story that you have in your head of just it's the World Cup national teams competing to see who's going to win.

00:12:08.220 --> 00:12:20.780
Does this kind of game ever need a story like how Punch Out kind of had like between rounds or between not rounds, but between different circuits, you would see the training and everything.

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:22.900
Does it does it need a little flavor like that?

00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:33.880
It doesn't have to go like if you recall in one of our Nostalgia Bites episodes, we did Captain Tsubasa, which was like an anime soccer game with crazy cut scenes and everything.

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:38.160
It doesn't have to go that far, but does it need a little something to drive the player?

00:12:38.720 --> 00:12:42.860
I feel kind of like I'm missing out on this.

00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:46.920
I like when sports games go.

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:52.880
Don't try and man in no world is this game trying to be a simulation, but it is trying to be a sports.

00:12:52.900 --> 00:12:56.800
And I really like it when sports games try to be something else.

00:12:57.100 --> 00:13:00.300
Like that's why I've mentioned it before on the podcast.

00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:11.320
But like Blitz the League is a game in which a story, not a great story, but like it's not just a franchise mode in a football game.

00:13:11.320 --> 00:13:20.860
It is a story in which your stupid team ends up playing in a very corrupt league and all that kind of stuff.

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:40.240
I would have liked to see the high school tournament mode in this game instead of what ends up being a kind of goofy version of soccer and having the audacity to call it World Cup when it doesn't even have offsides.

00:13:40.240 --> 00:13:47.800
I prefer the more fun cartoony version where it makes sense to play with the rules and stuff.

00:13:48.820 --> 00:13:50.820
So, yeah, I like that kind of stuff.

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:52.620
Yeah, for sure.

00:13:52.760 --> 00:13:56.420
And I mean, it's leaning into it in gameplay, so it might as well have it.

00:13:56.420 --> 00:14:04.100
But the core gameplay loop, we're not going to explain the rules of soccer here, but just explain how they translate soccer.

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:07.620
We mentioned all the there are no rules thing, but there's still time.

00:14:08.140 --> 00:14:11.520
So there's about time still exists.

00:14:12.060 --> 00:14:14.160
There's two halves, four minutes each.

00:14:14.900 --> 00:14:18.780
There are five players on the field on each side.

00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:22.480
It's five V five. That is not how real soccer is.

00:14:22.600 --> 00:14:25.220
I believe real soccer is 11 on each side.

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:31.260
I don't think the game needed to go to that level, especially because one, it's not trying to be a sim.

00:14:31.440 --> 00:14:32.420
It is arcadey.

00:14:32.500 --> 00:14:33.780
It is fun. It is silly.

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:38.620
I think the five on five is the appropriate way because of the sizing of the screen.

00:14:38.620 --> 00:14:45.920
They made it so that you don't have this vertical scroll in addition to a horizontal scroll because the field is so big.

00:14:46.020 --> 00:14:51.380
They kept it so that it's all just kind of, you know, it does.

00:14:51.380 --> 00:14:57.680
It does vertically scroll, obviously, but not like in a way where you can't see the immediate action in front of you.

00:14:58.020 --> 00:15:05.800
Yeah. The other thing you only control one player on the team.

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:11.800
So the whole time it's there's no button to like switch over.

00:15:12.140 --> 00:15:13.840
That's very strange over one of the computer.

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:14.900
Yes, I agree.

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:20.900
But I think they did that because they wanted to make one button a pass and one button a shoot.

00:15:21.140 --> 00:15:30.780
And because of the super shot taking A and B together, I just can't think of another button combination for them to do to give you control of another player.

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:34.080
So all you do is, I mean, we've already solved this problem.

00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:38.400
You just sort of, oh, I see what you mean.

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:41.500
It would also be used to pass to you.

00:15:42.400 --> 00:15:52.180
Yes. But you could say, you could say what I thought you were going to say is when you, whoever, as soon as the computer gains control of the ball, then you become that person.

00:15:52.360 --> 00:15:55.160
Yeah. Then the pass button becomes changed person.

00:15:55.860 --> 00:15:59.360
Right. So we've done it before.

00:15:59.360 --> 00:16:06.720
I think it makes a lot more sense if you're going to have some kind of story and you're only playing as one person like canonically.

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:13.540
And I'm not sure how the original game plays or if that is the case.

00:16:14.300 --> 00:16:16.500
But it seems like a holdover of that.

00:16:17.480 --> 00:16:21.300
In which case, I think it would make sense if like your character is one guy.

00:16:21.720 --> 00:16:28.920
However, this is a national team and there's no main character on the national team.

00:16:29.120 --> 00:16:30.480
So I think it's weird.

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:31.300
Right.

00:16:31.460 --> 00:16:38.760
And we know it's possible to control other characters on the field at the same time because the game actually allows up to four players at once.

00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:45.600
So it's not like there is some coding rule for why it's like you can only be this one character.

00:16:46.060 --> 00:16:56.320
Sean, you mentioned that the knocked out players, for lack of a better word, the incapacitated players, they stay incapacitated on the field.

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:58.060
Nobody comes to retrieve them.

00:16:58.060 --> 00:17:01.360
Pretty metal. Nobody swaps out, right, either.

00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:04.300
There's not like, okay, he's injured, so get somebody from the bench.

00:17:05.400 --> 00:17:08.520
Now that's just where they lay until the end of the half.

00:17:08.900 --> 00:17:14.780
So that creates the, to make another hockey term here, like a power play.

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:25.940
Basically, you could have a six on five, a six on four, a six on two situation if you're ruthless enough to take everybody else out.

00:17:26.260 --> 00:17:27.740
Yeah, I think it stops.

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:39.100
I think you, like, there needs to be two people on the opposing team or it wouldn't be, not that it even think, they're even thinking about fairness here.

00:17:39.100 --> 00:17:42.820
But I think it's a limit to losing three players.

00:17:43.160 --> 00:17:46.320
But still, like, they don't get back up.

00:17:46.420 --> 00:17:47.800
Like, there's no stoppage in play.

00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:49.540
So you don't get them back.

00:17:49.640 --> 00:17:52.120
I think you get them back at the half, maybe.

00:17:52.120 --> 00:18:02.680
But otherwise, it's way too, it's way too punishing if you're gonna, especially if we're playing against each other.

00:18:02.980 --> 00:18:05.620
And we just keep losing guys.

00:18:05.820 --> 00:18:07.800
I think that's just a frustration engine.

00:18:09.160 --> 00:18:12.080
Yeah. Do you think that any of these guys are faking it?

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:15.060
Like, they're hoping to draw a card?

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:17.880
Hey, that's how you fix diving.

00:18:17.880 --> 00:18:21.060
You just get rid of any kind of referees.

00:18:21.920 --> 00:18:22.780
Right, right.

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:26.140
So no, they're actually in dire pain.

00:18:27.340 --> 00:18:34.340
And, you know, the power play component of it, I think, is actually the interesting part of it.

00:18:34.440 --> 00:18:48.700
It's one thing to incapacitate a player, but to actually change the balance of the two teams, knocking the player out and having it be like, yes, I could see it being frustrating if, you know, you're playing against somebody else and you are literally handicapped down to two people.

00:18:48.700 --> 00:18:57.060
However, I've got to think that, like, that's part of everyone's strategy is also just, like, how fast can I knock out the other guy's players?

00:18:57.220 --> 00:19:03.060
Like, maybe I don't even give a shit about the ball for a little bit and I'm just tackling everybody I can.

00:19:03.440 --> 00:19:09.240
Spot me five goals while you try and break all their legs and then make it up on the back end.

00:19:09.620 --> 00:19:10.980
Well, that's another thing, Sean.

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:12.520
