00:19:12.680 --> 00:19:14.140
These games get out of hand.

00:19:14.340 --> 00:19:17.300
Yeah. They are unrealistic scoring for soccer.

00:19:17.300 --> 00:19:18.160
I know that much.

00:19:18.160 --> 00:19:22.720
I don't think I've ever seen anybody score more than seven goals in a game.

00:19:22.880 --> 00:19:26.160
I think it was that Brazil.

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:29.560
Was it Germany? It was Germany-Brazil, that World Cup game.

00:19:29.620 --> 00:19:33.400
Do you remember that? I have never watched the World Cup.

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:40.200
I'm pretty sure Germany scored, like, seven goals against Brazil in, like, the first ten minutes of the game.

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:43.320
And it was like, everybody was worried about the Brazilian team.

00:19:43.460 --> 00:19:44.840
Like, are they going to be able to come home?

00:19:45.000 --> 00:19:46.340
I don't think they would.

00:19:47.060 --> 00:19:49.360
Yeah. They're still there, right?

00:19:49.940 --> 00:19:52.000
I think it was 2016, that World Cup.

00:19:52.240 --> 00:19:53.860
Okay. Maybe 2014.

00:19:55.700 --> 00:19:57.400
Maybe 2018.

00:19:57.980 --> 00:20:00.780
Yeah. Yeah, definitely an even number.

00:20:03.140 --> 00:20:05.900
But I haven't seen a game that high scoring.

00:20:05.900 --> 00:20:10.520
But every game of this that I played was this high scoring.

00:20:10.520 --> 00:20:13.720
Because, also, you don't even need to do special shots.

00:20:13.740 --> 00:20:24.300
You can kind of juke the goalie pretty easily just by doing little twirls in that little crease area.

00:20:25.380 --> 00:20:26.920
And guaranteed goal.

00:20:27.880 --> 00:20:30.660
Yeah. Juking the goalie is kind of the only way, too.

00:20:30.740 --> 00:20:34.760
Because if you don't do that, the goalie will almost certainly block your shot.

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:38.460
You know? Even a super shot?

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:45.320
No, no. I guess I just mean, like, if you just take a shot directly at the net, like, the goalie's going to block it.

00:20:45.320 --> 00:20:53.120
Like, you need to do something with your shot in order to make it so that it doesn't just, like, there's not enough.

00:20:53.400 --> 00:20:58.700
There is no limit to how close to the net you can be, which I know is also a rule in soccer.

00:20:58.880 --> 00:21:01.140
Like, you do have to be outside of that box.

00:21:01.680 --> 00:21:03.500
Do you? Yeah, you do.

00:21:04.020 --> 00:21:05.200
I didn't think so.

00:21:05.340 --> 00:21:06.980
But okay. I think to take the shot, you do.

00:21:07.460 --> 00:21:14.880
I've seen, but I've seen, like, highlights of soccer matches where the guy's just, like, there.

00:21:15.760 --> 00:21:19.900
That's true. Maybe there's, like, a rule of, like, because, you know, like, it's like an offsides thing.

00:21:20.020 --> 00:21:21.580
Like, you can't be parked in there.

00:21:21.640 --> 00:21:22.480
You can't be parked.

00:21:22.980 --> 00:21:25.380
You have to take the ball with you into that zone.

00:21:25.480 --> 00:21:27.680
That makes more sense. That does make more sense.

00:21:28.240 --> 00:21:34.120
It's a little important that I learn these rules before World Cup 2026.

00:21:34.980 --> 00:21:36.620
Is it? It is.

00:21:36.900 --> 00:21:39.000
Because I'm, no, I'm definitely not going to go.

00:21:39.300 --> 00:21:40.740
Have you seen those ticket prices?

00:21:42.140 --> 00:21:46.560
But it's funny because it's, like, in our backyard and we can't, like, I can't even see it with binoculars.

00:21:47.540 --> 00:21:53.640
But meanwhile, I don't, I just feel like this is the one time to get excited about soccer for somebody who's not.

00:21:53.900 --> 00:21:55.100
I think you're right.

00:21:55.340 --> 00:22:05.600
I would say if you really want to get into soccer, you got to watch, like, the, like, didn't we just do?

00:22:05.700 --> 00:22:07.580
Conca Calf or however you say it?

00:22:07.780 --> 00:22:12.360
Like, when all the American countries kind of yell at each other?

00:22:12.820 --> 00:22:18.660
Excuse me? Look that up on your own time.

00:22:18.840 --> 00:22:20.060
I think. Conca Calf.

00:22:20.180 --> 00:22:24.480
Okay. Yeah. It's, you know, all the European people, like, are out of the way.

00:22:24.680 --> 00:22:26.500
They've got their own way to play soccer.

00:22:26.860 --> 00:22:34.440
It's when Brazil and all those teams get to, like, get to kick the shit out of the Americans and Canadians.

00:22:35.100 --> 00:22:36.980
That's when all the fun stuff happens.

00:22:37.260 --> 00:22:42.680
The fun stuff might just be limited to beating the shit out of players and the super shots.

00:22:42.880 --> 00:22:44.300
But the super shots also have a limit.

00:22:44.420 --> 00:22:48.060
Just like you can't knock out an entire team and cause a forfeit.

00:22:48.100 --> 00:22:51.200
You can only use five super shots per half.

00:22:51.360 --> 00:22:54.560
And that's probably necessary as well, right?

00:22:55.800 --> 00:22:59.720
Sounds pretty arbitrary considering everything else they let you get away with.

00:22:59.720 --> 00:23:02.280
But, sure, it's probably for the best.

00:23:03.040 --> 00:23:07.980
Yeah. But there are some play elements in the versus mode.

00:23:07.980 --> 00:23:13.520
If you leave the tournament, you do get the ability to play on other types of turf, not just grass.

00:23:13.520 --> 00:23:17.040
You can select between grass, sand, dirt, and ice.

00:23:17.440 --> 00:23:21.900
Each one obviously changing the traction and ball behavior.

00:23:22.180 --> 00:23:28.240
I don't think the players are more slippery on ice, but I didn't play on the ice either, so I can't confirm that.

00:23:29.000 --> 00:23:48.700
But one neat little trick here, if you do a verse match on, let's say, the sand, and then you finish that match and go into tournament mode while the game, without ever resetting or turning it off, you will inherit that field type in the tournament mode.

00:23:48.800 --> 00:23:50.340
Wow, that sounds like a huge mistake.

00:23:50.860 --> 00:23:54.240
Yeah. I don't think it was intended, but it definitely happens.

00:23:54.240 --> 00:24:00.820
They just don't have a way to reset the field type unless you choose grass again in verse mode.

00:24:00.840 --> 00:24:02.720
I think that should sort of be a thing.

00:24:02.840 --> 00:24:10.280
If you're hosting the World Cup, you should be able to make all of the fields ice.

00:24:11.420 --> 00:24:13.120
That should be within your right.

00:24:13.300 --> 00:24:21.540
Kind of how in the Olympics you get to pick whatever not real sports you're going to make sports just so you can get some medals.

00:24:21.540 --> 00:24:30.580
You should be able to force all of these world-class athletes to play soccer on ice.

00:24:31.600 --> 00:24:37.480
Right, right. Now, before each game, there's a couple boxes you have to tick.

00:24:37.900 --> 00:24:41.660
They basically work as on-off switches or yes-nos.

00:24:41.880 --> 00:24:42.980
Strategy. Yeah.

00:24:44.060 --> 00:24:52.700
And those strategy things of how you want to play offensive or defensive, how aggressively your teammates go for tackles versus shots.

00:24:54.940 --> 00:25:14.680
It's a smart way, I think, of, especially to an audience that might not be too familiar with soccer, of communicating strategy to these, you know, especially for assigning to your computer, rather than having to control all of the players and executing that play style all on your own.

00:25:15.480 --> 00:25:27.300
Yeah, I mean, again, I would prefer to just be able to play as whoever, but if you're going to force me to stay locked to one guy, this is a good way to at least customize how you want to play.

00:25:27.480 --> 00:25:36.680
Instead of just saying pass to me over and over just so that you can finally take control of the game.

00:25:46.320 --> 00:26:23.560
See you next time. And then the other thing you get to do besides setting up the strategies is you get to choose which six players from each team's roster get fielded, but there's no stats.

00:26:23.740 --> 00:26:24.560
Like, there are stats.

00:26:24.680 --> 00:26:27.640
The manual mentions that all players have their own characteristics.

00:26:27.900 --> 00:26:30.600
So why wouldn't you include the stats somewhere?

00:26:30.820 --> 00:26:32.640
Why does that have to be a mystery?

00:26:32.860 --> 00:26:34.060
You got to fill it out.

00:26:34.280 --> 00:26:36.160
You got to play it over and over.

00:26:36.440 --> 00:26:44.420
Yeah. How many games do you how many matches do you think it would take you to figure out like specific characters to like who is who?

00:26:44.680 --> 00:26:52.760
Yeah. You know, I understand the idea of like figuring out all the different super shots across the team so that you don't just play as the USA every game.

00:26:52.800 --> 00:26:59.640
But to figure out like who that guy specifically was and where he is on the field when he's behaving that way.

00:26:59.720 --> 00:27:04.640
And if he actually moves faster or shoots harder, I don't buy that.

00:27:04.640 --> 00:27:10.120
Yeah. I mean, at least they all have specific like faces, which is nice.

00:27:11.420 --> 00:27:13.500
I mean, I think they get like that.

00:27:13.620 --> 00:27:22.540
They're kind of duplicated between teams, but I think per team, they all have unique, unique faces so that you are right on both accounts.

00:27:22.780 --> 00:27:25.120
Yeah. So you would figure it out eventually.

00:27:25.480 --> 00:27:31.300
Like, oh, the guy that just has a huge circly eyes is probably Frank.

00:27:33.360 --> 00:27:42.260
But I don't think that I'm paying attention enough or ever to be able to say I'm going to sub in Lucas.

00:27:42.900 --> 00:27:47.700
Right. The versus match, as I mentioned, can go up to four players.

00:27:47.920 --> 00:27:50.980
It's also one of those interesting games where you can play three player.

00:27:51.300 --> 00:27:53.540
You don't have to have either two or four.

00:27:53.540 --> 00:27:57.660
It does allow you to do 2v1 as well with the rest being computer.

00:27:58.140 --> 00:28:07.020
But the four players simultaneously with the NES four score was a big sell of this game in all promotional material, but also in the manual.

00:28:07.020 --> 00:28:16.360
It straight up tells you to buy the NES four square four score or the NES satellite, which is basically the wireless version of the four score.

00:28:16.660 --> 00:28:28.400
I can't imagine buying a wireless controller product in, you know, back in 1990 and hoping for like a an input lag free experience.

00:28:28.540 --> 00:28:30.600
I'm sure there's no lag at all.

00:28:30.740 --> 00:28:34.840
I'm sure that it gets interfered with by a hairdryer.

00:28:35.120 --> 00:28:35.960
But OK.

00:28:36.200 --> 00:28:51.340
Yeah. But all that to say, like, this makes a little more sense for why Nintendo of America or and Nintendo as a whole is like getting involved here and rebranding this game that they didn't even really make.

00:28:51.520 --> 00:29:02.460
You know, they're they're borrowing Technos Japan's game and saying like, hey, let's localize this and get a reason to sell the four score in America.

00:29:02.680 --> 00:29:05.200
Right. Like to do during World Cup fever.

00:29:05.200 --> 00:29:06.760
For USA is finally back.

00:29:07.240 --> 00:29:09.120
Four player soccer is where it's at.

00:29:09.760 --> 00:29:19.860
And you just for the cozy price of buying a four score, which was probably like 50 bucks and this game, which was probably like 40 bucks or 50 bucks.

00:29:20.340 --> 00:29:21.440
You could do that.

00:29:22.460 --> 00:29:23.320
Would you?

00:29:23.320 --> 00:29:24.560
I wouldn't.

00:29:24.660 --> 00:29:26.600
But that's going to leave me to my next topic.

00:29:26.760 --> 00:29:30.740
So thank you, Sean. Is that when you don't care about the sport, right?

00:29:32.320 --> 00:29:36.520
How how hard is it for you to get into the video game version of it?

