00:30:21.580 --> 00:30:25.120
So, no, I mean, this is fun.

00:30:25.140 --> 00:30:26.680
I liked it.

00:30:27.020 --> 00:30:35.120
Yeah. And I think in general, I'm weirdly like with soccer, I need it to not be like a sim game.

00:30:35.120 --> 00:30:35.920
Yeah.

00:30:36.140 --> 00:30:52.400
When it gets to like a full scale giant field, like you said, knowing the formations and the strategy stuff, it's like I love hockey and I can barely play the NHL games, the modern ones correctly because of just like, you know, I'm not I'm no coach.

00:30:52.620 --> 00:31:02.900
I have no I'm just like running around, skating around on the ice, hoping that I don't, you know, that I can get over without doing an icing or something.

00:31:02.900 --> 00:31:09.860
So all that to say is like, I think for me, I can be interested in any sports game, too.

00:31:10.060 --> 00:31:21.940
But the ones that I don't the ones I'm not super familiar with, I feel like I need the the more arcadey like light on the rules version of the game.

00:31:22.080 --> 00:31:26.840
So this is way more approachable to me than the FIFA games are.

00:31:27.520 --> 00:31:40.540
Absolutely. On the if I call it sequels and spinoffs, there was a Game Boy version of this game with just some trimmed features.

00:31:40.540 --> 00:31:52.920
But the the Cuneo version of this game also came out on PC Engine and Mega Drive, which is the Genesis in other countries.

00:31:53.360 --> 00:31:58.020
And all those things are just like expanded teams, better graphics.

00:31:58.020 --> 00:32:01.320
The CD version has an arranged soundtrack.

00:32:02.560 --> 00:32:05.840
Nothing like nothing that changes the core experience.

00:32:05.980 --> 00:32:07.440
Nobody ever added rules.

00:32:07.760 --> 00:32:09.520
Nobody ever added referees.

00:32:09.760 --> 00:32:20.960
No one made the you know, if anything, they just made the the soccer longer, like the time and the ability to like play soccer and all that.

00:32:20.960 --> 00:32:27.620
But the the game did not like get a follow up, though, for for North America.

