00:33:23.680 --> 00:33:35.120
There were a lot of other World Cup games, though, that didn't, you know, for other systems, home computers, arcades, Mega Drive, that I'm not going to go like too in depth on.

00:33:35.120 --> 00:33:43.380
But just to throw out their names, there's Tecmo World Cup 1990, World Cup Soccer Italia 90, Kickoff 2.

00:33:43.380 --> 00:33:55.140
The one thing that all three of these games that I mentioned have in common is that they all go for the sim aspect where it's like, obviously, the graphics are still either 8 or 16 bit.

00:33:55.140 --> 00:34:03.280
But they have like a top-down realistic view with the 11 on 11 approach.

00:34:03.460 --> 00:34:08.940
And they try to best give those, you know, some will have still no fouls.

00:34:09.020 --> 00:34:14.060
Others will have like, you know, different, not all the players on the field.

00:34:14.060 --> 00:34:27.680
But the idea is that Nintendo is the only one who's leaning into like this fun, chibi style of soccer that's like a little more carefree and probably better suited for video games in 1990.

00:34:28.000 --> 00:34:30.560
Like, it's great that these other ones exist for the purists.

00:34:30.560 --> 00:34:37.260
But I feel like out of all of them, from a video game fun standpoint, Nintendo gets that best.

00:34:37.300 --> 00:34:40.540
And that's why they chose what they went with for the localization.

00:34:41.600 --> 00:34:44.520
Still feel like, again, just feel like we're missing out.

00:34:44.800 --> 00:34:54.020
Well, we might be missing out, Sean, but we won't let our listeners miss out on this final section, the essential games list.

00:34:58.520 --> 00:35:01.840
I think Nintendo World Cup is a smart move by Nintendo.

00:35:02.360 --> 00:35:08.180
If I'm putting on like my marketing hat and everything, like, sure, soccer isn't the biggest thing.

00:35:08.340 --> 00:35:16.260
But I can totally see this from the four-player standpoint, the arcade-y nature, the quick gameplay, too.

00:35:16.380 --> 00:35:18.880
It does not take long to do one of these matches.

00:35:18.880 --> 00:35:26.020
So even playing with a friend or having multiple friends around, even if you don't have the four-score, you can kind of like quickly get in a bunch of games.

00:35:26.080 --> 00:35:31.720
I could see all that working and this being fondly remembered by the people who grew up with it.

00:35:31.740 --> 00:35:33.340
But I think that's where it stays.

00:35:34.140 --> 00:35:40.320
I don't know if it's like – it's not even anything about the controls or anything like that.

00:35:40.320 --> 00:35:54.080
But I think it's just what I want from like a soccer game isn't going to happen on like 8-bit because I haven't even seen it happen on the modern games like I was talking about with the FIFA games.

00:35:54.140 --> 00:35:59.140
Like, I'm not sure I've found the kind of thing I'm looking for in a soccer game to like recommend it.

00:35:59.140 --> 00:36:12.120
The closest thing I can think of is maybe like, you know, Football Manager where it's like, damn, they really went all in on owning a club and building it out year over year over year.

00:36:12.280 --> 00:36:22.360
And like that's the kind of thing that's a totally different kind of sports game but still falls into that same like scratching the itch as the simulation games of today do.

00:36:22.360 --> 00:36:31.520
So that's going to be like my recommendation having only spent minutes in those games that are supposed to be hundreds of hours is maybe start there.

00:36:31.720 --> 00:36:33.660
Sean? Yeah.

00:36:33.900 --> 00:36:42.140
